    "notes": "Hussein bin Talal was proclaimed King of the Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan on 11 August 1952 and remained king until his death on 7 February 1999. A Regency Council exercised the royal functions until he assumed his constitutional powers on 2 May 1953; ATLAS nevertheless records the recognized royal reign as 1952–1999."
